Haakon Studebaker wrote:
> I'd like to suggest that gray dragon scales and gray dragon scale mail are 
> much tougher to enchant than normal dragon armor. Same goes with converting 
> it to scale mail rather than scales.
> A blessed scroll will guarantee a +1 enchantment while a normal scroll of 
> enchant armor would have a 25% chance of enchanting the armor.

There have been many games where not a single dragon left scales to enchant.
Even being not very tough I had faced every fight to work hard for my scale
mail. Once, after every possible/likely place (throne rooms, Ludios, Castle)
is cleared without any scales I tend to use a single wish from the Castle
wand to get it.

Do we need to make enchanting scales to armor more difficult? The problem
is rarely that you don't have enough scrolls at that point; if you can use
a single scroll to enchant the scales you can as well use (at average) four.
I think currently it's complex enough to manufacture the scales (compared
to simple wishing for the +2 thing); you have to kill a tough creature (and
spend one additional scroll to get the mail from the scales).

Do we need to let it cost more scrolls to get the +0 scale mail to +4 ?
In this case I'd enchant my other about five(!) pieces of armor. Why should
I bother enchanting the scale mail if it's costly?

Frankly, if you have a point it's not apparent to me; would you mind to
elaborate about your thoughts?

